course: dictionary
lesson: 10018
title: The number ten
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ten is the number 10, and it is one more than nine. It is the base of our number system, so we count in tens. Ten ones make one ten, and ten tens make one hundred.
explain: «A squid or cuttlefish has eight arms plus two longer tentacles, ten limbs in all.» You can check this with adding: eight plus two makes ten. Ten fingers and ten toes work the same way, and they are a handy way to count to ten.
explain: When you multiply a number by 10, every digit moves one place to the left. So 3 tens are 30, and 7 tens are 70. Try it yourself: what is 4 tens?
fact: Ten is the number 10, one more than nine.
fact: Ten ones make one ten, and ten tens make 100.
fact: To multiply by 10, move each digit one place to the left: 6 × 10 = 60.
fact: Ten is the base of our number system, which is why we count in tens.
fact: «Ten out of ten» means full marks.
exercise: «A squid has eight arms plus two longer tentacles, ten limbs in all.» How many limbs in all? | *10 | 12 | 20 | 8
exercise: What is 4 tens? | 4 | 14 | 104 | *40
exercise: What is 10 × 6? | 16 | *60 | 6 | 600
test: How many ones make one ten? | 1 | 100 | 5 | *10
test: What is 9 + 1? | 1 | 8 | *10 | 11
exam: What is 10 tens? | *100 | 1000 | 1 | 10
